  3596	                                Appendix II. Some special cases
  3597	
  3598	      A simple Computer program shows that the only possible counter-examples to the
  3599	Jacobian conjecture for polynomials of degrees less than 100 are of degrees (64, 68),
  3600	(84, 56), (75, 50) and (99, 66) with some special data attached. A routine computation
  3601	shows that the numbers of coefficients of the pairs of polynomials involved are 3370,
  3602	5308, 4352 and 7348 respectively. The task of direct verification of the Jacobian con-
  3603	jecture by computation for those pairs of polynomials with the said degrees is beyond
  3604	the capacity of a large Computer. In this Appendix we shall illustrate some methods to
  3605	reduce the numbers of coefficients, and then settle the problems of computations.
