   424	## 5. Branch C: exact exclusion in the declared radius-two ODE system
   425	
   426	If `H` has three simple roots, resonance is impossible because `2r=25` has no
   427	integer solution.  Equation (4.1) forces multiplicity 14 at each root, hence
   428	`deg R>=42`, contradicting `deg R=40`.  This kills C under the radius-two
   429	`T_3`-leader premise just typed.
   430	
   431	For a coefficient-system check, work on the squarefree stratum.  If
   432	`R=H^jR_j`, then (4.1) becomes
   433	
   434	```text
   435	2H R_j' +(2j-25)H'R_j = k H^(14-j).
   436	```
   437	
   438	For `j=0,...,12`, reduction modulo `H` shows `H|R_j`: the integers
   439	`2j-25` are nonzero and `H'` is a unit modulo squarefree `H`.  Thus
   440	`R=H^13L`.  Scale `R`, hence `L`, to be monic and absorb that nonzero scalar
   441	into `k`; then `L` is monic linear and the remaining necessary equation is
   442	
   443	```text
   444	H'L+2HL'-kH=0.                                                (5.1)
   445	```
   446	
   447	Normalize `H=z(z-a)(z-b)`, `L=z+ell`.  The four coefficients of (5.1) are
   448	
   449	```text
   450	f1=5-k,
   451	f2=(k-4)(a+b)+3ell,
   452	f3=(3-k)ab-2(a+b)ell,
   453	f4=ab ell.
   454	```
   455	
   456	The ring is `Q[a,b,ell,k,T]`; the squarefree/nonzero stratum is selected by
   457	`f5=T*ab(a-b)k-1`.  Singular returns `[1]` in each of `F_32003`, `F_32009`,
   458	`F_32027`, and `Q`, in under 0.014 seconds per run.  Each run passed the empty
   459	wrapper, nonempty wrapper, and unsaturated-nonunit controls.
   460	
   461	`CERTIFICATE-SIZE`: one polynomial in the reduced basis.  An independently
   462	expanded rational certificate has five summands and maximum multiplier total
   463	degree 7.  Put `s=a+b`, `p=ab`, `d=a-b`; then
   464	
